## 2. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp` — `GgufFile::find()` is O(n) per lookup

**Responsibilities.** `find(name)` returns the first `TensorInfo` with a given name; `GgufModel` already builds a `std::map` index across shards, but the single-file `GgufFile` used by `ple.cpp`, `strata-gguf`, and the parity tools linearly scans `tensors_`.

**Problem.** The PLE table open path (`PleTable::open`) and `check_experts_gguf` call `find()` repeatedly while validating hundreds of tensor names against a 1,223-entry directory; each call is a full string-compare scan. On the Unsloth 4-shard model the per-role validation in `expert_source.cpp` performs thousands of lookups. A lazily built `std::map<std::string, size_t>` index turns each into O(log n) with no API change.

**Change.**

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp
@@
     const TensorInfo* find(const std::string& name) const {
-        for (const auto& t : tensors_)
-            if (t.name == name) return &t;
-        return nullptr;
+        if (index_.empty() && !index_built_) build_index();
+        const auto it = index_.find(name);
+        return it == index_.end() ? nullptr : &tensors_[it->second];
     }
@@
     void parse() {
         ...
         data_start_ = (c.pos() + align - 1) / align * align;
         if (data_start_ > size_) throw std::runtime_error("GGUF: data section starts past EOF");
+        build_index();   // the directory is final here; a duplicate name already threw above
     }
+    void build_index() const {
+        index_.reserve(tensors_.size());
+        for (size_t i = 0; i < tensors_.size(); ++i) index_.emplace(tensors_[i].name, i);
+        index_built_ = true;
+    }

     std::string path_;
     ...
     std::vector<TensorInfo> tensors_;
     std::map<std::string, MetaValue> meta_;
+    mutable std::map<std::string, size_t> index_;
+    mutable bool index_built_ = false;
 };
```

**Verification.**
1. `gguf_reader_test` and `gguf_split_test` must still pass unchanged (same `find()` results, same duplicate-name refusal).
2. Micro-benchmark in `src/artifact/gguf_reader_test.cpp`: time 10,000 `find()` calls on the tiny model before and after; assert the new path is faster and returns identical pointers.

