## 3. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths()` silently accepts non-numeric shard numbers

**Responsibilities.** Resolves any shard path of a split model to the full ordered shard list, throwing when a shard is missing.

**Problem.** The digit loop `for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i)` checks `a < '0' || a > '9'` for the shard number and total, but the *extension* check `any.compare(at + 9, 5, ".gguf")` is only reached after the length check `any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5`. A path like `model-00001-of-00002.GGUF` (uppercase) or `model-00001-of-00002.gguf.bak` falls through to `return {any}` — treated as a one-shard model — and the caller then opens a file that is shard 1 of N with no metadata (Unsloth's case) and fails much later with a confusing "no general.architecture" error. The function should distinguish "not a split name" from "a split name with an unexpected suffix" and warn.

**Change.**

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@
     static const char tag[] = "-of-";
     const size_t at = any.rfind(tag);
     // "...-NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf": five digits before the tag, five after it, then the extension
-    if (at == std::string::npos || at < 6 || any[at - 6] != '-' || any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5 ||
-        any.compare(at + 9, 5, ".gguf") != 0)
+    if (at == std::string::npos || at < 6 || any[at - 6] != '-')
         return {any};
     int no = 0, n = 0;
     for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
         const char a = any[at - 5 + i], b = any[at + 4 + i];
         if (a < '0' || a > '9' || b < '0' || b > '9') return {any};
         no = no * 10 + (a - '0');
         n = n * 10 + (b - '0');
     }
     if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n) return {any};
+    // The digits say "split model" but the tail is not ".gguf": almost certainly a renamed or
+    // partially downloaded file.  Say so instead of opening one shard of a multi-shard model.
+    if (any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5 || any.compare(at + 9, 5, ".gguf") != 0)
+        throw std::runtime_error("model file " + any + " looks like shard " + std::to_string(no) + " of " +
+                                 std::to_string(n) + " but does not end in .gguf - check the file name");
     std::vector<std::string> out;
```

**Verification.**
1. `gguf_split_test`: add a case `model-00001-of-00002.gguf.tmp` (file exists) → expect `std::runtime_error` naming the file; previously it returned a one-element vector.
2. Existing cases (valid split, single file, `model-00001-of-0000a.gguf` non-digit) must keep their current behavior: the non-digit case still returns `{any}`.

