## 6. `include/strata/core/conversation_memory.hpp` — `conversation_mem_available` has no declaration for its parsing contract

**Responsibilities.** Parses `/proc/meminfo`'s `MemAvailable` into bytes; `conversation_memory_admit` gates snapshot allocation on it.

**Problem.** The header declares `conversation_mem_available(std::istream&)` but the implementation lives in `src/core/conversation_memory.cpp` (not shown), and the header gives no contract for the units or the failure mode. The `std::optional` return distinguishes "unknown" from "zero", but a malformed line (`MemAvailable:  abc kB`) must not be read as zero. The header should document the exact accepted grammar so a future parser change cannot silently turn "unknown" into "0 available" (which would disable parking on every Linux host).

**Change.**

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/conversation_memory.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/conversation_memory.hpp
@@
 // Host physical memory, not swap/commit or a container/job memory reservation.
 // Unknown telemetry is deliberately distinct from a measured zero.
 std::optional<uint64_t> conversation_available_memory();
+/// Parses one line of /proc/meminfo text: `MemAvailable:  <digits> kB`.  Returns the value in BYTES,
+/// or std::nullopt when the line is absent, the number is not pure digits, or the kB multiplier is
+/// missing.  A malformed line is nullopt (unknown), NEVER 0: a parse failure must not read as
+/// "no memory" and silently disable conversation parking on every Linux host.
 std::optional<uint64_t> conversation_mem_available(std::istream& meminfo);
```

